=begin
  libeo: the shared library for the e-scripts.

  Loaded once per session with Script.loadlib('libeo'); definitions persist after the
  library script exits. Script.loadlib never loads it twice, so a script that needs a newer
  copy than the session holds runs libeo again. Then it names the version it was built
  against and the library refuses a mismatch loudly:

    Script.loadlib('libeo')
    Script.run('libeo') if Gem::Version.new(::EO::VERSION) < Gem::Version.new('0.13.0')
    EO.require('0.13.0')

  This file only loads the library. The library itself is scripts/eo/, one file per
  concern; each file opens with what it holds, and README.md has the list.

        author: elanthia-online
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: Gemstone
          tags: library, utility, eo
      required: Lich >= 5.22.0
       version: 0.13.0

  Version Control:
  Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  v0.13.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Herbs::Heal, from eherbs 2.3.0: the herb to use for a type from what the sack
      holds (find, treats?, in_hand), the spells that help (cast_spells), eating or
      drinking one (use), and what to pass over when none was found (skip_for)
    - EO::Herbs::Shop, from eherbs 2.3.0: the herbalist's menu and what on it treats a
      type (menu, on_menu), ordering and buying (order, buy), a price (price,
      entry_for), what a place sells and what the sack holds for a heading (location,
      sold, held, doses), and bundling (bundle_all)
  v0.12.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Herbs::Doses::Monitor, from eherbs 2.3.0: the doses left in each herb and
      potion, read from the game's lines as they are used, measured, bought and
      bundled, and kept in $eherbs_measure
    - EO::Herbs::Sack, from eherbs 2.3.0: the herb sack's OPEN, LOOK, PUT and GET answers,
      opening it (open), its contents by form (by_form), a Survivalist's Kit's
      (kit_contents), those of something in the room (room_contents, in_room), putting
      a herb in and taking one out (put, take, free_hand, free_hands)
  v0.11.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Herbs::Table, from eherbs 2.3.0: every herb with where it is sold, what it
      treats and its doses (KNOWN), the stock targets (DEFAULT_DOSES), the two tiers of
      blood (major_blood?, blood_tier, blood_bucket, in_category?), where herbs are sold
      (sold_at?), and what is drunk or cannot be bundled (DRINKABLE, CANT_BUNDLE)
    - EO::Herbs::Injuries, from eherbs 2.3.0: the herb type a character's wounds call for
      next (next_type), what a dead character or an escort needs from how the game
      describes them (appraise, escort), the character's condition by type (status),
      and whether wounds allow a spell (able_to_cast?)
  v0.10.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Cleanse::Wounds, from ecleanse 2.4.0: whether wounds and scars allow a cast, as
      they are and under Sigil of Determination (allow_cast?, allow_cast_with_sigil?),
      and changing stance (stance)
    - EO::Cleanse::Afflictions: curing disease and poison (cure_disease, cure_poison),
      retreating from a root or press (retreat), dispelling debuffs (dispel_debuffs),
      the ways out of a stun and of a web (stun_means, break_stun, stun_maneuver,
      web_escape?, break_web), quieting a room (settle_room)
    - EO::Cleanse::Recovery: getting a lost weapon back: calming the room (calm,
      stop_calm), the spirit servant (servant), a bonded weapon (await_bonded), RECOVER
      ITEM (search, restore_hands), prying one from webbing (pry), one floated away
      (float_back), the Sanctum's clench (clench)
  v0.9.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Cleanse, from ecleanse 2.4.0: the debuffs and room hazards by name, the spell a
      character has for each job (spell), TARGET and its answers (target), the mana
      pulse (mana_pulse), and the hazards that would not be targeted (BadTargets)
    - EO::Cleanse::Hazards: getting rid of a web, globe or cloud by spell, Spell Cleave
      or Spell Thieve (clear), blowing acidic mist away (blow_away), breaking a
      runestone (shatter)
    - EO::Cleanse::Traps: the Hive's traps searched out and disarmed (search, disarm,
      here?), and the itchy curse's safe place and wait (safe_place, wait_out_rash)
    - EO::Cleanse::Disarms: a weapon back in hand (recovered?, held_ids), the list of
      disarms not yet recovered, kept across restarts (list, add, remove, remove_room,
      remove_found, tracked?), and reading RECOVER ITEM (spied_item, same_item?)
  v0.8.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Casting, from ewaggle 2.2.0: the multicast count by mana control
      (max_multicast), one cast and what its answer means (cast), having the mana or
      stamina for it and making mana by Sign of Wracking, Sigil of Power or Symbol of
      Mana (ready, ready_stamina, Resources, safe_to_wrack?, wander_step), another
      character's active spells (active_on), and manna bread (new_in_hand, gobble)
  v0.7.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Locker, from eloot 2.15.0: a house's locker rooms by the map's tags (che_rooms,
      che_town_id, town_name), LOCKER INFO's town (info_town), rooms nearest first
      (nearest_first), the way into a booth and the last step to one (way, booth?,
      approach, step), what came since a reading (lines_since), a debt (debt), opening
      the locker and finding the stash in it (open, stash, here, inside?)
    - EO::Hoard, from eloot 2.15.0: one name for a label and an item (normalize), whether
      a name is of the kind hoarded (kind?), a stash's inventory by looking in each jar
      or from a premium locker's manifest (inventory, manifest_town, manifest_inventory,
      read_jar, refresh), filtering it (filter), the jar for a name and shaking one
      (jar_of, shake, jar_in_hand)
  v0.6.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Selling, from eloot 2.15.0: SELL one item and the refusals (sell), APPRAISE and
      the figure in its answer (appraise, worth)
    - EO::Locksmith, from eloot 2.15.0: how the town locksmith is called (town_activator),
      a box shut or locked (shut?, locked?), the call, the fee and the PAY (call, fee,
      pay), and the nouns he will not open
    - EO::Locksmith::Pool, from eloot 2.15.0: the drop-off order (order), the give and the
      ask for a return (give, ask_return, returned_box), the pool's depth from its list
      (depth, counts), and the rising tip (tip_for, tip)
  v0.5.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Stow, from eloot 2.15.0: the bags an item is tried in by the STOW list (route),
      the overflow bags in number order (overflow_keys), the bags to open before looting
      (bags_for)
    - EO::Loot, from eloot 2.15.0: what in a room is no loot (junk?, with the name, noun
      and disk lists), whether an item is wanted (wanted?, CATEGORIES), a list as one
      whole-word pattern (words), and LOOT on a dead creature (search, in_hand?, bramble?)
    - EO::Skinning, from eloot 2.15.0: which dead to leave (skip?, sometimes?), a
      bounty's creature (for_bounty), edged or blunt (by_tool), getting ready (prepare),
      the SKIN (skin), standing up after (stand_up)
  v0.4.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Town, from eloot 2.15.0: Four Winds Isle and the way off it (fwi?, leave_fwi),
      the shop to walk to and whether to go (shop_elsewhere?, nearest_shop), a shop in a
      bounty's town within the region (in_region), the trash receptacle (trash_can), the
      locksmith pool's worker (pool_worker)
    - EO::Items, from eloot 2.15.0: MARK's unsellable (marked?), throwing an item away
      (toss), phasing a box and bringing it back (phase, unphase), lifting a curse by 315
      or an eonake gauntlet (lift_curse), waiting for the disk (await_disk)
    - EO::Boxes, from eloot 2.15.0: opening a box, looking in, taking coins once and the
      answers to it, and which emptied box is kept (keep?)
  v0.3.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Containers, from eloot 2.15.0: the OPEN, LOOK IN and CLOSE answers, whether
      Lich has a container's contents (listed?), opening one that does not (ensure_open),
      waiting for contents (contents_ready?), reading them fresh (fresh_contents), close
    - EO::Hands, from eloot 2.15.0: the GET and PUT answers, what the hands hold
      (holding?), freeing one (free_hand), taking an item (take), wearing one (wear),
      putting one in a container (store), and the READY list's STORE and READY
      (stow_ready, return_ready, ready_word)
  v0.2.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO.use: a script lends the library its own helpers (command, result, wait, go,
      say, and any other by name), and EO.command, EO.result, EO.settle, EO.go2 and
      EO.say call the running script's. Code that moves here from a script goes on
      sending, waiting, walking and printing that script's way
  v0.1.0 (2026-11-13)
    - the loader and the version gate: EO.require, EO.version
=end

# The library's files, in the order they load: a file may use what an
# earlier one defines.
parts = %w[
  version helpers containers hands town items boxes stow loot skinning selling locksmith locker hoard casting
  cleanse/tables cleanse/hazards cleanse/traps cleanse/disarms
  cleanse/wounds cleanse/afflictions cleanse/recovery
  herbs/table herbs/injuries herbs/doses herbs/sack herbs/heal herbs/shop
]

base = File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'eo')
verbose = $VERBOSE
begin
  # a second run in a session redefines every constant; that is the point
  $VERBOSE = nil
  parts.each { |part| load File.join(base, "#{part}.rb") }
ensure
  $VERBOSE = verbose
end
